<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<worksheet>
  <title>33: Contour integrals</title>

  <exercise workspace="3.5in">
    <introduction>
      <p>Evaluate <m>\int_C z~dz</m> where</p>
    </introduction>
    <task workspace="1in">
      <statement>
        <p><m>C</m> is the straight line from <m>0</m> to <m>1+i</m>.</p>
      </statement>
    </task>
    <task workspace="1in">
      <statement>
        <p><m>C</m> is the contour consisting of straight line segments from
  <m>0</m> to <m>1</m> and from <m>1</m> to <m>1+i</m>.</p>
      </statement>
    </task>
  </exercise>

  <exercise workspace="1.5in">
    <task workspace="3in">
      <statement>
        <p>Evaluate <m>\oint_C \overline{z}~dz</m> where <m>C</m> is the unit square
  (<m>0\leq x \leq 1</m> and <m>0\leq y \leq 1</m>)
  traversed in the counterclockwise direction.</p>
      </statement>
    </task>
    <task workspace="1in">
      <statement>
        <p>Suppose that <m>C</m> is a closed contour bounding a region whose area is
  <m>A</m>.  Use Green's theorem to explain why <m>\oint_C \overline{z}~dz =
  2iA</m>.</p>
      </statement>
    </task>
  </exercise>

  <exercise workspace="2in">
    <introduction>
      <p>Suppose that <m>C</m> is the unit circle traversed in the
  counterclockwise direction.</p>
    </introduction>
    <task workspace="3in">
      <statement>
        <p>Parameterize the unit circle as <m>z(t) =
  e^{it}</m> to evaluate</p>
        <p>\begin{enumerate}
  \item <m>\oint_C z~dz</m>.</p>
        <p>\item <m>\oint_C z^3~dz</m>.</p>
        <p>\item <m>\oint_C \frac1z~dz</m>.</p>
        <p>\item <m>\oint_C \frac1{z^3}~dz</m>.
\end{enumerate}</p>
      </statement>
    </task>
    <task workspace="2in">
      <statement>
        <p>What is the general rule for <m>\oint_Cz^n~dz</m>?</p>
      </statement>
    </task>
    <task workspace="1in">
      <statement>
        <p>Now suppose that <m>C</m> is the circle of radius <m>R</m> centered at the
  origin parametrized as <m>z(t) = Re^{it}</m>.  What do you find for
  <m>\oint_C z^n~dz</m>?</p>
      </statement>
    </task>
  </exercise>

  <exercise>
    <introduction>
      <p>Suppose that <m>C</m> is a closed contour and that <m>f(z)</m> is complex
  differentiable in the region <m>D</m> inside <m>C</m>.</p>
    </introduction>
    <task workspace="3in">
      <statement>
        <p>Write <m>\oint_C f(z)~dz</m> as a line integral in terms of <m>dx</m> and
  <m>dy</m>.  Then apply the Green's Theorem to evaluate the contour
  integral.  What do you find for the value of <m>\oint_Cf(z)~dz</m>?</p>
      </statement>
    </task>
    <task workspace="1.5in">
      <statement>
        <p>On the first page, you evaluated <m>\oint_C \overline{z}~dz</m> around
  the unit square.  Explain why your result shows that <m>\overline{z}</m>
  is not complex differntiable.</p>
      </statement>
    </task>
    <task workspace="1in">
      <statement>
        <p>Since <m>z^n</m> is differentiable if <m>n\geq 0</m>, give another
  explanation for why <m>\oint_C z^n = 0</m> if <m>C</m> is the unit circle.</p>
      </statement>
    </task>
  </exercise>

</worksheet>
